---
import CalculatorLayout from '../layouts/CalculatorLayout.astro';
import NtuCgpaCalculatorWidget from '../components/calculators/NtuCgpaCalculator';

const relatedCalculators = [
  { title: "NTU Grade Calculator", path: "/ntu-grade-calculator" },
  { title: "NUS CAP Calculator", path: "/nus-cap-calculator" },
  { title: "SMU GPA Calculator", path: "/smu-gpa-calculator" },
];
---

<CalculatorLayout
  title="NTU CGPA Calculator"
  description="Calculate your Cumulative Grade Point Average (CGPA) for Nanyang Technological University (NTU). Includes S/U handling and exact degree classifications."
  category="Academic & Education"
  categoryPath="/categories/academic"
>
  <NtuCgpaCalculatorWidget client:load slot="calculator" />

  <Fragment slot="content">
    <h2>How to use the NTU CGPA Calculator</h2>
    <p>
      The <strong>NTU Cumulative Grade Point Average (CGPA)</strong> is the standard metric used to measure academic performance at Nanyang Technological University. Our calculator allows you to quickly project your semester GPA and your overall CGPA.
    </p>
    <p>
      To use the calculator:
    </p>
    <ol>
      <li><strong>(Optional) Enter your current standing:</strong> Input your current CGPA and the total number of graded Academic Units (AUs) you have accumulated.</li>
      <li><strong>Add your current semester courses:</strong> For each course, enter the AUs and your expected grade.</li>
      <li><strong>S/U Options:</strong> If you are using the Satisfactory/Unsatisfactory (S/U) option, select 'S' or 'U'. These grades do not affect your CGPA, but an 'S' grade will award you the AUs needed for graduation.</li>
    </ol>
    <p>
      The tool will automatically display your expected CGPA, your GPA for the current semester, and your projected Honours classification based on NTU's official guidelines.
    </p>

    <h3>NTU Grade Points Table</h3>
    <p>NTU follows a 5.0 grade point system:</p>
    <ul>
      <li><strong>A+ / A:</strong> 5.0</li>
      <li><strong>A-:</strong> 4.5</li>
      <li><strong>B+:</strong> 4.0</li>
      <li><strong>B:</strong> 3.5</li>
      <li><strong>B-:</strong> 3.0</li>
      <li><strong>C+:</strong> 2.5</li>
      <li><strong>C:</strong> 2.0</li>
      <li><strong>D+:</strong> 1.5</li>
      <li><strong>D:</strong> 1.0</li>
      <li><strong>F:</strong> 0.0</li>
    </ul>

    <h3>NTU Degree Classification (Honours)</h3>
    <p>For students admitted from AY2018 onwards, degrees are classified as follows:</p>
    <ul>
      <li><strong>Highest Distinction:</strong> CGPA 4.50 - 5.00</li>
      <li><strong>Distinction:</strong> CGPA 4.00 - 4.49</li>
      <li><strong>Merit:</strong> CGPA 3.50 - 3.99</li>
      <li><strong>Honours:</strong> CGPA 3.00 - 3.49</li>
      <li><strong>Pass:</strong> CGPA 2.00 - 2.99</li>
    </ul>
    <p><em>Note: Students need a minimum CGPA of 2.00 to satisfy graduation requirements.</em></p>
  </Fragment>

  <Fragment slot="faq">
    <div class="space-y-4">
      <details class="group bg-slate-50 dark:bg-slate-800/50 p-4 rounded-lg">
        <summary class="font-medium cursor-pointer list-none flex justify-between items-center text-slate-900 dark:text-slate-100">
          Does an A+ give more points than an A?
          <span class="transition group-open:rotate-180">
            <svg fill="none" height="24" shape-rendering="geometricPrecision" stroke="currentColor" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" stroke-width="1.5" viewBox="0 0 24 24" width="24"><path d="M6 9l6 6 6-6"></path></svg>
          </span>
        </summary>
        <p class="text-slate-600 dark:text-slate-300 mt-3">
          No. Both A+ and A carry a grade point of 5.0 in the calculation of your CGPA.
        </p>
      </details>
      <details class="group bg-slate-50 dark:bg-slate-800/50 p-4 rounded-lg">
        <summary class="font-medium cursor-pointer list-none flex justify-between items-center text-slate-900 dark:text-slate-100">
          How do S/U courses work?
          <span class="transition group-open:rotate-180">
            <svg fill="none" height="24" shape-rendering="geometricPrecision" stroke="currentColor" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" stroke-width="1.5" viewBox="0 0 24 24" width="24"><path d="M6 9l6 6 6-6"></path></svg>
          </span>
        </summary>
        <p class="text-slate-600 dark:text-slate-300 mt-3">
          S/U courses are excluded from your CGPA calculation. If you get an 'S' (Satisfactory), you earn the Academic Units (AUs). If you get a 'U' (Unsatisfactory), you do not earn the AUs, but your CGPA remains unaffected.
        </p>
      </details>
      <details class="group bg-slate-50 dark:bg-slate-800/50 p-4 rounded-lg">
        <summary class="font-medium cursor-pointer list-none flex justify-between items-center text-slate-900 dark:text-slate-100">
          What happens if I fail a course (F grade)?
          <span class="transition group-open:rotate-180">
            <svg fill="none" height="24" shape-rendering="geometricPrecision" stroke="currentColor" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" stroke-width="1.5" viewBox="0 0 24 24" width="24"><path d="M6 9l6 6 6-6"></path></svg>
          </span>
        </summary>
        <p class="text-slate-600 dark:text-slate-300 mt-3">
          An 'F' grade carries 0.0 grade points. The AUs for the failed course will be counted in the denominator of your CGPA calculation, which will pull your CGPA down.
        </p>
      </details>
    </div>
  </Fragment>

  <Fragment slot="related">
    {relatedCalculators.map(calc => (
      <li>
        <a href={calc.path} class="group flex items-center p-2 rounded-md hover:bg-white dark:hover:bg-slate-700 transition-colors">
          <svg class="w-4 h-4 mr-2 text-slate-400 group-hover:text-teal-500" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" viewBox="0 0 24 24"><path stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" stroke-width="2" d="M9 5l7 7-7 7"></path></svg>
          <span class="text-sm font-medium text-slate-700 dark:text-slate-300 group-hover:text-teal-600 dark:group-hover:text-teal-400">{calc.title}</span>
        </a>
      </li>
    ))}
  </Fragment>
</CalculatorLayout>
